# Data and integration rules

- Treat Google Sheets, CMSs, CRMs, feeds, and AI APIs as typed external systems with explicit contracts.
- Validate and normalize external records before they reach presentation components.
- Keep credentials server-side. Use environment variables and least-privilege service accounts.
- Add timeouts, actionable errors, retry behavior where appropriate, and a safe fallback for temporary upstream failure.
- Define caching and freshness intentionally. Surface a last-updated value when freshness matters to users.
- Avoid direct spreadsheet-cell assumptions throughout the UI. Map source rows into stable domain objects in one adapter.
- Log enough context to diagnose failures without logging secrets or sensitive user data.
- When a site is powered by an operational data source, make that benefit visible in the experience: explain what can be updated, by whom, and how quickly changes appear.
